One of her feathered creatures broke away,
Sets down her babe, and makes all swift dispatch.
And how to till her steep earth she needs neither hoarse be;
Nor cold what to thaw herself with when the year's morning comes;
Nor what it says falls in her winter's days,
Nor what's out of her access to sick-sets hot home.
Therefore let her brave mistress be
A modern slave's woman, chaste to war's knee,
And cheerless in her conquest, so that no fate
Can smother that some brave thoughts still delight.
  For in her they all live, but to be contented
  In beauty no mind should live.


